From f4d38f30c54cf7869c9d9fa224c10de26fb9751f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Bozik <robertbozik@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] libcamera: software_isp: Gather zone statistics and
 meter the centre

The statistics are a single histogram and a single set of sums for the
whole frame, so the AGC has no notion of where the light is: a window
behind the subject wins and the subject goes black.

Accumulate the sampled pixels into a 16x9 grid of zones (sums and
counts) and gather a second luminance histogram over the central zones.
Let the tuning file set meteringCentreWeight: the mean sample value is
then taken from a blend of the whole frame and the centre, and the
highlight protection looks at the centre only, so that the background
is allowed to clip. The default of 0 keeps the whole-frame metering.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5 [Claude Code]
